  ],
  "recorded_scientific_conclusion": "The collision-off characteristic/upwind comparison is finite, algebraically closed and monotonic on 8x8, 16x16 and 32x32 grids. At 32x32 the first-order upwind bottom-wall average heat-flux bias is 1.0383577186540085%, below the preregistered 10% material threshold, while the full distribution weighted relative L1 error is 3.491412106165172%. Therefore collision-off first-order transport diffusion is not large enough by itself to explain the greater-than-25% finite-Kn heat-flux discrepancy retained from Stage 59. No physical, collision, transport, wall, normalization or velocity-quadrature parameter was retuned, and cross-Knudsen extension remains prohibited.",
